Converting Number to String - O(Number of digits) Time and O(Number of digits) Space  We can convert the number into a string and then find the length of the string to get the number of digits in the original number. If the number is negative, the string will contain a '-' sign, so subtract 1 from the length.
            C++

    #include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int countDigit(int n)
{
    // Convert integer to string
    string num = to_string(n);

    // If negative, exclude '-' sign
    if (num[0] == '-')
        return num.length() - 1;

    return num.length();
}

int main()
{
    int n = -58964;
    cout << countDigit(n); 
    return 0;
}


